IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cidra-types`
IMPORT `cidra-misrepresentation`

-- Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (UK) — GOAL 3:
-- THE INSURER'S REMEDIES (s 4(3), Schedule 1 Part 1).
--
--   "What may the insurer do: avoid the contract, keep or return the
--    premiums, rewrite the terms, cut the claim, or end the contract?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2012-6.txt — Schedule 1 Part 1.
-- The conversion drops the paragraph numbers; they are, in order, paras 1-9.
-- Each answer is the most the insurer may do: para 6 applies "if the insurer
-- so requires", and paras 7 and 9 say "may".

§ `Goal 3 — the insurer's remedies`

DECLARE `Remedy` HAS
    `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `premiums to return`                                IS A NUMBER
    `contract treated as on the different terms`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount payable on the claim`                       IS A NUMBER
    `may give notice of its rights for the future`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `may terminate by reasonable notice`                IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Sch 1 para 9(6): once the insurer gives notice under 9(4)(a), the
    -- consumer may terminate by reasonable notice (added after the
    -- independent pass; not barred for life insurance).
    `consumer may terminate after the insurer's notice` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Sch 1 para 8 "“Reduce proportionately” means that the insurer need pay on
-- the claim only X% of what it would otherwise have been under an obligation
-- to pay under the terms of the contract (or, if applicable, under the
-- different terms provided for by virtue of paragraph 6), where— X =
-- (Premium actually charged ÷ Higher premium) × 100".
@ref Sch 1 paras 7-8
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, charged IS A NUMBER, higher IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the claim` amount `reduced proportionately from` charged `to` higher MEANS
    amount TIMES (charged DIVIDED BY higher)

-- Sch 1 para 2 "If a qualifying misrepresentation was deliberate or reckless,
-- the insurer— (a) may avoid the contract and refuse all claims, and (b) need
-- not return any of the premiums paid, except to the extent (if any) that it
-- would be unfair to the consumer to retain them." The part returned is at
-- most the premiums paid (capped after the independent pass).
@ref Sch 1 para 2
GIVEN x IS A `Money facts`
GIVETH A `Remedy`
`the remedy for a deliberate or reckless misrepresentation with` x MEANS
    `Remedy` OF TRUE, `the lesser of` (x's `premiums unfair to retain`) (x's `the premiums paid`), FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Sch 1 paras 4-9, for a careless qualifying misrepresentation.
--   para 5 "If the insurer would not have entered into the consumer insurance
--     contract on any terms, the insurer may avoid the contract and refuse
--     all claims, but must return the premiums paid."
--   para 6: different terms (other than the premium) apply "if the insurer so
--     requires".
--   para 7: a higher premium — "the insurer may reduce proportionately the
--     amount to be paid on a claim".
--   para 9(4) "If ... the insurer would have either (or both) of the rights
--     conferred by paragraph 6 or 7, the insurer may— (a) give notice to that
--     effect to the consumer, or (b) terminate the contract by giving
--     reasonable notice"; (5) not "if it is wholly or mainly one of life
--     insurance".
@ref Sch 1 paras 3-9
GIVEN k IS A `Contract facts`, w IS A `What the insurer would have done`, x IS A `Money facts`
GIVETH A `Remedy`
`the remedy for a careless misrepresentation in` k `given` w `and` x MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `no contract on any terms` THEN
        `Remedy` OF TRUE, x's `the premiums paid`, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
    WHEN `the contract, on these terms` different higher THEN
        `Remedy` OF FALSE, 0, different, payable different higher, TRUE, NOT (k's `wholly or mainly life insurance`), TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        `Remedy` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, x's `the claim under the actual terms`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
    WHERE
        GIVEN different IS A BOOLEAN, higher IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        payable different higher MEANS
            IF   higher GREATER THAN x's `the premium actually charged`
            THEN `the claim` (base different) `reduced proportionately from` (x's `the premium actually charged`) `to` higher
            ELSE base different
        GIVEN different IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        base different MEANS
            IF   different
            THEN x's `the claim under the different terms`
            ELSE x's `the claim under the actual terms`

-- s 4(1), (3): without a qualifying misrepresentation the insurer has no
-- remedy: the claim is paid under the contract's terms.
@ref s 4(1), (3), Sch 1 Part 1
@export What the insurer may do under s 4 and Schedule 1 Part 1 of the Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (UK) about a consumer's misrepresentation before a contract: with no qualifying misrepresentation, nothing (the claim is paid in full); deliberate or reckless, avoid the contract, refuse all claims and keep the premiums except any it would be unfair to keep; careless, avoid and return the premiums if it would not have contracted at all, otherwise apply the different terms and pay the claim reduced in proportion of the premium charged to the higher premium, and give notice or (except for life insurance) terminate by reasonable notice for the future. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Contract facts`                     @desc Whether the contract is wholly or mainly life insurance
      m IS A `Misrepresentation facts`            @desc The misrepresentation, the care taken, and what the consumer knew
      w IS A `What the insurer would have done`   @desc What the insurer would have done without it
      x IS A `Money facts`                        @desc Premiums charged and paid, the claim under the actual and the different terms, and any premiums unfair to retain
GIVETH A `Remedy`
`the insurer's remedy for` k `and` m `given` w `and` x MEANS
    IF   `is a qualifying misrepresentation` m `given` w `and` x
    THEN CONSIDER `the class of` m
         WHEN `deliberate or reckless` THEN `the remedy for a deliberate or reckless misrepresentation with` x
         WHEN `careless` THEN `the remedy for a careless misrepresentation in` k `given` w `and` x
    ELSE `Remedy` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, x's `the claim under the actual terms`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
